--- !u!114 &768335760
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 768335758}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'TRUCK TERRIER RACING

    Twelve physical trucks on a diagonal, gently
    descending triangular course. Start wide and converge toward the one finish box.
    Animated track runners can be bowled into ragdolls; they do not score. Snow accumulates
    and actual tires cut Weatherade tracks. Up to four local humans; AI fills the
    remaining stalls. First to FIVE heat wins takes the match. All stalls rotate
    fairly between heats. Each heat uses a reproducible passable hurdle layout and
    one shared random weather field.


    DRIVE with your movement source. Opposite
    throttle brakes, then reverses. ACTION jumps only while grounded with a short
    cooldown: keyboard key shown in setup, whole-pad SOUTH, shared-left LT, shared-right
    RT. Every racer has identical NWH traction, power, jump and weather. Time jumps
    a little before each hurdle and converge toward the finish opening.


    THE
    TUNNEL: only a complete front-entry then rear-exit through the finish hole (25%
    wider opening) counts. Going over, around, or sideways into the barrier never
    wins. A high incoming wall-normal speed explodes the truck once; a gentle graze
    does not. The inner tunnel side faces are safe to brush; tiny physical contact
    tolerances cannot invalidate a genuine complete crossing. Only the official winner
    coasts off the exit into the colossal ice-cream bowl, with a real soft landing
    and squish. The opening closes behind the confirmed winner. Losing trucks fall
    toward the molten crater; lava contact produces impact effects and safely collects
    wreck pieces. Every ordinary wreck throws actual cab, chassis, doors and wheels
    as bounded physical pieces, also recorded in replay. Blasts can tumble neighbors.
    A locked legal finish is preserved against later debris. Missing a jump and remaining
    blocked for 1.1 seconds explodes the truck. After the first legal finish, the
    winner is locked and the heat continues for eight seconds to show the landing
    and remaining crashes before automatically ending. True simultaneous first finishes
    rerun with no point; all wrecked or 28 seconds without a legal finish also rerun.
    Repeated failures use the validated gentler fallback. No artificial winner.


    CAMERAS:
    In Truck gives each human a stable driver seat; AI uses no human viewport. Shared
    Broadcast shows the whole action. Eliminated drivers follow a live competitor.
    Every heat has a recorded nonphysical broadcast replay with launch and decisive
    finish/crash segments, angles, slow/fast speed, rewind and skip after one second.
    Replay cannot change the result. AI sessions advance automatically.


    Pause/disconnect
    preserves the heat and replay. Reconnect or explicitly replace, release controls
    and confirm freshly. Configuration persists through rematches. Offline only.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: be1034cebd9fa3643a48d11ef76e4708, type: 2}
